# Material graph nodes

Generated by `player --material-graph-schema`; see docs/MaterialGraph.md for the file format.
A float connects to any vector by repeating; `any` pins take the node's own type, the
widest of what's connected to them.

| Node | Values | Inputs | Outputs | What it does |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `constant` | 1 to 4 numbers |  | `out` any | A fixed number, vec2, vec3 or vec4 |
| `param` | name, then 1 to 4 numbers (its default) |  | `out` any | A named value a .swmaterial can change with "graph_param <name> <values>" |
| `texture` | "path", then "linear" for data (normals, masks) | `uv` vec2 (optional) | `rgba` vec4, `rgb` vec3, `r` float, `g` float, `b` float, `a` float | A texture from Content, read at uv (default: the mesh's first UV set) |
| `uv` | 0 or 1 (default 0) |  | `out` vec2 | The mesh's texture coordinates |
| `world_position` |  |  | `out` vec3 | The surface's position in the world, in metres |
| `world_normal` |  |  | `out` vec3 | The surface's normal in the world, before any normal map |
| `vertex_color` |  |  | `rgba` vec4, `rgb` vec3 | The mesh's vertex colour |
| `time` |  |  | `out` float | Seconds on the game's frame clock (repeats under --fixed-step) |
| `add` |  | `a` any, `b` any | `out` any | a + b |
| `subtract` |  | `a` any, `b` any | `out` any | a - b |
| `multiply` |  | `a` any, `b` any | `out` any | a * b, per component |
| `divide` |  | `a` any, `b` any | `out` any | a / b, per component |
| `lerp` |  | `a` any, `b` any, `t` any | `out` any | a where t is 0, b where it's 1 |
| `clamp` |  | `x` any, `min` any (optional), `max` any (optional) | `out` any | x kept within min (0) and max (1) |
| `saturate` |  | `x` any | `out` any | x kept within 0 and 1 |
| `power` |  | `a` any, `b` any | `out` any | a to the power b (a below 0 counts as 0) |
| `one_minus` |  | `x` any | `out` any | 1 - x |
| `dot` |  | `a` any, `b` any | `out` float | The dot product of a and b |
| `normalize` |  | `x` any | `out` any | x scaled to length 1 |
| `split` |  | `x` any | `r` float, `g` float, `b` float, `a` float | x's components (missing ones are 0, a missing alpha 1) |
| `combine` |  | `r` float, `g` float, `b` float (optional), `a` float (optional) | `rgba` vec4, `rgb` vec3, `rg` vec2 | Numbers put together into a vector (b defaults to 0, a to 1) |
| `fresnel` |  | `power` float (optional) | `out` float | 0 facing the camera, rising to 1 at grazing angles: (1 - n.v) to the power (default 5) |
| `noise` |  | `uv` vec2 | `out` float | Smooth value noise of uv, 0 to 1, one cell per unit |
| `panner` |  | `uv` vec2 (optional), `speed` vec2 | `out` vec2 | uv (default: the mesh's first UV set) plus time times speed: scrolling textures |
| `normal_blend` |  | `a` vec3, `b` vec3 | `out` vec3 | Tangent-space normal b laid over a (reoriented normal mapping) |

## Outputs

| Output | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `base_color` | vec3 | Linear RGB |
| `opacity` | float | Alpha for alpha_mode blend (mask still cuts out with the base colour's alpha) |
| `normal` | vec3 | Tangent-space normal, blue up (a texture node marked linear reads one) |
| `roughness` | float | Perceptual roughness, 0 mirror to 1 matte |
| `metallic` | float | 0 dielectric to 1 metal |
| `emissive` | vec3 | Emitted light, linear RGB (replaces the material's) |
| `occlusion` | float | Darkens ambient light only, 1 none |

Limits: 256 nodes, 16 textures and 16 params per graph.
